 "source_instruction": "i need a heavy duty desk chair for my office.  get me one that is easy to assemble though.",
 "query": "I spent all last weekend digging up the overgrown raised beds out in my backyard, pulling out so many stubborn dandelion taproots my forearms were sore for three straight days afterward. I even found a half-buried rusted trowel and a handful of chipped old ceramic planter shards tucked under a thick mat of creeping ivy when I cleared the corner by the fence. The neighborhood squirrels kept perching on the fence rail the whole time, chittering like they were heckling my slow progress and hoarding the last of the fallen acorns from the big oak tree to hide in the beds I\u2019d just finished turning over. I\u2019ve heard home office chairs that are super easy to put together work really well, nothing with a ton of confusing parts that take forever to set up. I\u2019ve heard the ones that are solid enough for regular daily use work well for that kind of regular daily use, y\u2019know? I\u2019m sticking to a pretty tight budget, so I\u2019ve heard nothing that goes over my limit works well for that situation.",
